# Forensic fixtures are byte-exact evidence. Git's text/binary autodetection only
# scans the first 8000 bytes for a NUL, so a compressed image whose first NUL
# falls past that window is classified as TEXT and has its LF bytes rewritten to
# CRLF on checkout under core.autocrlf=true -- the default on GitHub's
# windows-latest runners. That silently corrupts the fixture before any test runs.
#
# Observed in this fleet: 7 of 15 hfsplus decmpfs fixtures mangled exactly this
# way, including compressed INPUTS and not just expected-output files.
tests/data/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
